        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: заблудиться",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "заблудиться (zabludítsya) — \"to get lost\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В старом городе мы быстро заблудились. V stárom górode my býstro zabludílis. We quickly got lost in the old town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Perfective. Future заблужусь, заблудишься."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "заблудиться (zabludítsya) is built from за-, блудить 'to wander, to stray' and -ся; EtymDB lists it with the sense 'to get lost'. The root is Proto-Slavic blǫdŭ (EtymDB), the same root as in блуждать (bluzhdát) 'to wander'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
