              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ориентироваться (oriyentírovatsya) — \"to find one's way, to get one's bearings\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В новом городе я плохо ориентируюсь. V nóvom górode ya plókho oriyentíruyus. I am bad at finding my way in a new town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective сориентироваться. Takes в + prepositional."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ориентироваться (oriyentírovatsya) is usually traced to French orienter 'to orient, to set facing north' (EtymDB), on Latin oriēns 'rising; the east' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
